{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1430868-about-lodges-in-forsaken2","id":1430868,"title":"About Lodges in Forsaken2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-03T08:27:47-08:00","id":1430868,"title":"About Lodges in Forsaken2","content":"I remember that the 3 main lodges of every tribe are introduced in The Pack, inside a box, but I'm not able to consult the book right now.<br /> Is there any kind of rule for the main lodges? Or are we supposed to use the 1ed benefits ? Like more gift lists, and so on, for the one who joins the lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T11:26:29-08:00","id":1430894,"title":"","content":"They work the same as regular lodges. One of them is given an example in the write-ups on the next few pages, the Lodge of Garm, a lodge pillar of the Blood Talons that seek out the greatest champions among werewolves to bring down.<br /> <br /> I believe a key part of the mechanics was trying to avoid things like exp discounts, and so lodges got a bunch of new mechanics they come with. While there's a bunch of lodge merits like Lodge Armory and Lodge Sorcery, lodges may or may not have those.<br /> <br /> At the least, lodges come with four things: a blessing, which is like a more powerful version of a pack's totem advantage. A lodge Aspiration, offering a new way to get beats. A new ban. And a new Sacred Hunt benefit (like the tribal ones, it's one you can choose when you're leading the Sacred Hunt rite) that tends to be focused and powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T14:14:18-08:00","id":1430912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1430868-about-lodges-in-forsaken2?p=1430894#post1430894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They work the same as regular lodges. One of them is given an example in the write-ups on the next few pages, the Lodge of Garm, a lodge pillar of the Blood Talons that seek out the greatest champions among werewolves to bring down.<br /> <br /> I believe a key part of the mechanics was trying to avoid things like exp discounts, and so lodges got a bunch of new mechanics they come with. While there's a bunch of lodge merits like Lodge Armory and Lodge Sorcery, lodges may or may not have those.<br /> <br /> At the least, lodges come with four things: a blessing, which is like a more powerful version of a pack's totem advantage. A lodge Aspiration, offering a new way to get beats. A new ban. And a new Sacred Hunt benefit (like the tribal ones, it's one you can choose when you're leading the Sacred Hunt rite) that tends to be focused and powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you suggest for the Iminir's Lodge of Thunder as blessing/aspiration/ban and sacred hunt?<br /> From the Pack , players and storytellers are supposed to create these kind of rules or are there any kind of ''lodges creation'' mechanics? Or do we have to wait for official rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T14:49:22-08:00","id":1430920,"title":"","content":"The Pack does have some limited details for constructing a Lodge on page 80, but I personally found the blog posts here and Chris Allen's patreon to be more useful.<br /> Though to be fair, the blessings look a lot like totem blessing for a pack.<br /> <br /> I am not overly familiar with the Lodge of Thunder; what are they about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T16:09:37-08:00","id":1430930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1430868-about-lodges-in-forsaken2?p=1430920#post1430920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not overly familiar with the Lodge of Thunder; what are they about?</div> </div> </div> </div>They hunt powerful Claimed, particularly Hive-Claimed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T16:17:14-08:00","id":1430931,"title":"","content":"The Pack offers guidance and examples (there's five made ones) but they're supposed to be kind of tilted towards your game, and can vary in size and scope. So one Lodge might be really powerful and offer a lot of bonuses usable anywhere, while a small, local lodge might only offer abilities that help out in a very specific situation, like a lodge that only exists in Chicago might offer an exceptional success on 3 when dealing with institutions of Chicago during a sacred hunt. While a sprawling international lodge that's been running around for thousands of years might have a unique power like the Garmir, who can sense powerful (high Primal Urge) werewolves and retain full Defense when making all-out attacks against them.<br /> <br /> The pillar lodges, like Thunder, tend towards pretty powerful, though. &quot;The Lodge of Thunder hunt the most powerful of Claimed, in particular the terrifying Hive-Claimed.&quot; So they're basically giant-slayers. Also, &quot;Rumors abound that the Lodge of Thunder practices Essence-alchemy and the ritual consumption of Hive-Claimed corpses.&quot; They might have a special rite for that ritual consumption, but you might also have a Sacred Hunt condition that allows them to temporarily (for a month, or until they need another Sacred Hunt) add Size or Health to themselves by taking it from claimed or hive-claimed prey they've taken down. Sort of like the Bone Shadow one, but instead of taking the preys Essence and dividing that up, you'd divide their Size (to represent how much you're eating) and get it as a bonus to something. Simpler benefits might be like being able to treat targets Size as smaller (not actually shrinking it) so you can do assorted combat and Gift abilities to them you normally wouldn't be able to. An aspiration might be to simply find a hive-claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T06:23:38-08:00","id":1430980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1430868-about-lodges-in-forsaken2?p=1430931#post1430931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pack offers guidance and examples (there's five made ones) but they're supposed to be kind of tilted towards your game, and can vary in size and scope. So one Lodge might be really powerful and offer a lot of bonuses usable anywhere, while a small, local lodge might only offer abilities that help out in a very specific situation, like a lodge that only exists in Chicago might offer an exceptional success on 3 when dealing with institutions of Chicago during a sacred hunt. While a sprawling international lodge that's been running around for thousands of years might have a unique power like the Garmir, who can sense powerful (high Primal Urge) werewolves and retain full Defense when making all-out attacks against them.<br /> <br /> The pillar lodges, like Thunder, tend towards pretty powerful, though. &quot;The Lodge of Thunder hunt the most powerful of Claimed, in particular the terrifying Hive-Claimed.&quot; So they're basically giant-slayers. Also, &quot;Rumors abound that the Lodge of Thunder practices Essence-alchemy and the ritual consumption of Hive-Claimed corpses.&quot; They might have a special rite for that ritual consumption, but you might also have a Sacred Hunt condition that allows them to temporarily (for a month, or until they need another Sacred Hunt) add Size or Health to themselves by taking it from claimed or hive-claimed prey they've taken down. Sort of like the Bone Shadow one, but instead of taking the preys Essence and dividing that up, you'd divide their Size (to represent how much you're eating) and get it as a bonus to something. Simpler benefits might be like being able to treat targets Size as smaller (not actually shrinking it) so you can do assorted combat and Gift abilities to them you normally wouldn't be able to. An aspiration might be to simply find a hive-claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Taking a look to the book right now, thanks for your answer.<br /> I see that the benefits are individual so basically, I can personalize the hunt style of my pc in order to hunt the lodge's favorite play using my best capabilities and skills.<br /> Amazing thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}